    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Unsigned index-to-coordinate conversion by reciprocal multiplication.\n2: \n3: Original synthetic Triton adaptation of fast integer divmod techniques.\n4: The output contains row/column coordinates for a width-seven layout.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: import torch\n7: import triton\n8: import triton.language as tl\n9: \n10: _DIVISOR = 7\n11: _SHIFT = 31 + (_DIVISOR - 1).bit_length()\n12: _MULTIPLIER = ((1 << _SHIFT) + _DIVISOR - 1) // _DIVISOR\n13: \n14: \n15: @triton.jit\n16: def _unflatten(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\n17:                MULTIPLIER: tl.constexpr, SHIFT: tl.constexpr):\n18:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n19:     active = index < N\n20:     value = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0).to(tl.uint64)\n21:     quotient = (value * MULTIPLIER) >> SHIFT\n22:     remainder = value - quotient * 7\n23:     tl.store(OUT + 2 * index, quotient.to(tl.uint32), mask=active)\n24:     tl.store(OUT + 2 * index + 1, remainder.to(tl.uint32), mask=active)\n25: \n26: \n27: def validate_inputs(indices, require_cuda=True):\n28:     \"\"\"Enforce the complete public domain, including uint32 extrema.\"\"\"\n29:     def require(condition, message):\n30:         if not condition:\n31:             raise ValueError(message)\n32: \n33:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n34:     require(type(indices) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n35:     require(indices.layout == torch.strided and indices.is_contiguous(),\n36:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n37:     require(not indices.requires_grad and not indices.is_inference(),\n38:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n39:     require(not indices.is_neg() and not indices.is_conj(),\n40:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n41:     require(not require_cuda or indices.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n42:     require(indices.ndim == 1 and 1 <= indices.numel() <= 131072,\n43:             \"indices must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n44:     require(indices.dtype == torch.uint32, \"uint32 input required\")\n45:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": indices.numel()}\n46: \n47: \n48: def run(indices):\n49:     \"\"\"Return unsigned row/column coordinates in a fresh [N,2] tensor.\"\"\"\n50:     validate_inputs(indices)\n51:     n = indices.numel()\n52:     with torch.cuda.device(indices.device):\n53:         output = torch.empty((n, 2), dtype=torch.uint32, device=indices.device)\n54:         _unflatten[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n55:             indices, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, MULTIPLIER=_MULTIPLIER,\n56:             SHIFT=_SHIFT, num_warps=4)\n57:     return output\n58: \n59: \n60: def reference(indices):\n61:     \"\"\"Exact direct integer division on an int64 widening of each uint32.\"\"\"\n62:     validate_inputs(indices, require_cuda=False)\n63:     values = indices.to(torch.int64)\n64:     rows = torch.div(values, 7, rounding_mode=\"floor\")\n65:     columns = torch.remainder(values, 7)\n66:     return torch.stack((rows, columns), dim=1).to(torch.uint32)\n67: \n68: \n69: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n70:     \"\"\"Convenience examples; all uint32 values belong to the input domain.\"\"\"\n71:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n72:     values = torch.randint(0, 1 << 32, (size,), dtype=torch.int64,\n73:                            generator=generator).to(torch.uint32)\n74:     return (values.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Decompose unsigned 32-bit linear indices into row and column coordinates\nfor a row-major layout with a fixed width of 7:\n\n  row[i] = floor(indices[i] / 7)\n  col[i] = indices[i] - 7 * row[i].\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- indices is a one-dimensional torch.uint32 tensor [N], 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY unsigned 32-bit value is legal, from 0 through 4294967295 inclusive.\n  Indices are values to decompose, not offsets used to access a backing\n  matrix; no matrix allocation or additional index-range bound is implied.\n- indices is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. It has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This is not an autograd\n  operation.\n\nReturn a fresh torch.uint32 tensor [N,2] on indices.device, with columns\n[row, col], preserving the input and its backing storage. Every coordinate\nmust equal the integer mathematical target EXACTLY. Floating-point or\napproximate tolerances are not used. In particular, every col is in [0,6]\nand 7*row + col equals the original unsigned index in mathematical integers.\n\nAny division method is allowed, including reciprocal multiplication,\nbit operations and precomputed constants, if it satisfies this exact\nrequirement for every legal unsigned index. Correctness is one verdict\nfor the whole implementation; changing inputs only supplies evidence.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nuses direct int64 division and remainder; it accepts CPU inputs. make_inputs()\nis a convenience generator, not an input-domain restriction. Index-to-coordinate\nconversion and precomputed fast division are standard GPU indexing operations.\nThis is an original synthetic Triton adaptation of reciprocal-division\ntechniques, not a claim of an upstream historical bug.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
